Cybersecurity Analyst &amp; Systems Security Engineer

🛠️ Technical Security Skills &amp; Tools
🟢 Network Scanning: Nmap
🟢 Exploitation: Metasploit
🟢 Traffic Analysis: Wireshark
🟢 SIEM &amp; Analytics: Splunk
🟢 Boundary Routing: pfSense / VPN
🟢 Testing: Black Box Testing
🚀 Cyber Range Portfolio Projects
Project 1: Black Box Hacking Simulation (Capstone)
Simulated a real-world defensive audit on a blind target environment. Researched hidden attack surfaces, ran stealth service tracking controls, exploited security gaps safely, and structured executive documentation briefs.

Core Phases Execution:
Reconnaissance &amp; Scanning: Used Nmap for passive asset mapping and service fingerprinting.
Packet Analysis: Tracked communication layers using Wireshark to locate system vulnerabilities.
Exploitation Sequence: Used Metasploit Framework vectors to achieve root authorization footprints.
Black Box Hacking Lab Screen📂 Download Presentation
Project 2: Enterprise Hybrid Lab &amp; Splunk SIEM Engineering
Designed a multi-site network lab within EVE-NG to evaluate zero-trust network layout boundaries. Simulated live Red Team penetration routing paths over an encrypted IPsec VPN tunnel while aggregating enterprise telemetry back to a central Splunk platform.

Core Phases Execution:
Network Isolation: Programmed pfSense firewalls to contain lateral host movement.
Offensive Auditing: Ran custom vulnerability sequences against target systems and corporate web elements.
Detection Engineering: Engineered specialized Splunk Processing Language (SPL) rules to trigger immediate alerts on live attacks.
EVE-NG Network Topology Map💻 View Splunk Configurations
