Project 1: Black Box Hacking Simulation (Capstone)
Simulated a real-world defensive audit on a blind target environment. Researched hidden attack surfaces, ran stealth service tracking controls, exploited security gaps safely, and structured executive documentation briefs.

Core Phases Execution:
Reconnaissance &amp; Scanning: Used Nmap for passive asset mapping and service fingerprinting.
Packet Analysis: Tracked communication layers using Wireshark to locate system vulnerabilities.
Exploitation Sequence: Used Metasploit Framework vectors to achieve root authorization footprints.
