"><div class="QRnEfb">Google may use account and system data to understand your feedback and improve our services, subject to our <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" class="c0nryc"><span class="sds-typography-utility__colorOnSurfaceLink" style="">Privacy Policy</span></a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" class="c0nryc"><span class="sds-typography-utility__colorOnSurfaceLink">Terms of Service</span></a>. For legal issues, <a href="https://support.google.com/legal/answer/3110420" target="_blank" class="c0nryc"><span class="sds-typography-utility__colorOnSurfaceLink">make a legal removal request</span></a>.</div></div></div><!--TgQPHd|||[114,{&quot;u&quot;:0},false,false]--></div></span></div></div><div data-zzy="1" data-processed="true"></div><!--TgQPHd|MnlGHc_1ij/DbG24d;MnlGHc_1ij/Qok6p;MnlGHc_1ij/ns9scf||[[1,0,0,null,0,0,1,&quot;7PqWavCUNaOh5NoPnIOPgQ4&quot;,null,null,0,0,0,0,0,1,&quot;Kofi Agyei\nCybersecurity Analyst \u0026 Systems Security Engineer\n\n🛠️ Technical Security Skills \u0026 Tools\n🟢 Network Scanning: Nmap\n🟢 Exploitation: Metasploit\n🟢 Traffic Analysis: Wireshark\n🟢 SIEM \u0026 Analytics: Splunk\n🟢 Boundary Routing: pfSense / VPN\n🟢 Testing: Black Box Testing\n🚀 Cyber Range Portfolio Projects\nProject 1: Black Box Hacking Simulation (Capstone)\nSimulated a real-world defensive audit on a blind target environment. Researched hidden attack surfaces, ran stealth service tracking controls, exploited security gaps safely, and structured executive documentation briefs.\n\nCore Phases Execution:\nReconnaissance \u0026 Scanning: Used Nmap for passive asset mapping and service fingerprinting.\nPacket Analysis: Tracked communication layers using Wireshark to locate system vulnerabilities.\nExploitation Sequence: Used Metasploit Framework vectors to achieve root authorization footprints.\nBlack Box Hacking Lab Screen📂 Download Presentation\nProject 2: Enterprise Hybrid Lab \u0026 Splunk SIEM Engineering\nDesigned a multi-site network lab within EVE-NG to evaluate zero-trust network layout boundaries. Simulated live Red Team penetration routing paths over an encrypted IPsec VPN tunnel while aggregating enterprise telemetry back to a central Splunk platform.\n\nCore Phases Execution:\nNetwork Isolation: Programmed pfSense firewalls to contain lateral host movement.\nOffensive Auditing: Ran custom vulnerability sequences against target systems and corporate web elements.\nDetection Engineering: Engineered specialized Splunk Processing Language (SPL) rules to trigger immediate alerts on live attacks.\nEVE-NG Network Topology Map💻 View Splunk Configurations\n📩 Connect With Me\nLooking for a dedicated Security Analyst? Let&#39;s talk!\n\nEmail: kofiagyei79@gmail.com\n\nGitHub Profile\n© 2026 Kofi Agyei Portfolio. Built with HTML5 \u0026 CSS3.  ,project one is able to open but project two is not able&quot;,0,0,null,0,0,0,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,null,null,&quot;/search/about-this-result?origin\u003dwww.google.com\u0026req\u003dCgASMwonCgIIcQohCF1iHQoMY291bnRyeV9uYW1lEg1Vbml0ZWQgU3RhdGVzEgQKAghlGgIIABoAIgIQAUgAWABoAA\u0026hl\u003den-US\u0026gl\u003dUS&quot;],&quot;https://www.google.com&quot;],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[null,1,null,null,null,null,null,null,3,[null,null,null,&quot;sge_&quot;,null,1,null,null,null,null,null,5297367,&quot;AIM&quot;,[null,null,[null,2],null,null,null,null,[[&quot;feedback_entrypoint&quot;,&quot;sge_msaf_action&quot;]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,&quot;MAGI_FEATURE&quot;,[&quot;&quot;,&quot;BLUR&quot;,0,0]],null,null,null,null,null,135,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,1,1,null,1]]],1,null,[null,&quot;[13,\&quot;Ac4dDhkDnOc_szwQUSGc5z971DPxTQz0v61dloU5DPS_\&quot;,\&quot;-8510670496035746955\&quot;,\&quot;0x89e40645d49beeb7:0xece79f82e1e60c7f\&quot;]&quot;,4]]]--></div></div