cstrong\u003eReconnaissance \u0026 Scanning:\u003c/strong\u003e Used Nmap for passive asset mapping and service fingerprinting.\u003c/li\u003e \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePacket Analysis:\u003c/strong\u003e Tracked communication layers using Wireshark to locate system vulnerabilities.\u003c/li\u003e \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExploitation Sequence:\u003c/strong\u003e Used Metasploit Framework vectors to achieve root authorization footprints.\u003c/li\u003e \u003c/ul\u003e \u003cimg class\u003d\&quot;project-image\&quot; src\u003d\&quot;black-box-hacking.png\&quot; alt\u003d\&quot;Black Box Hacking Lab Screen\&quot;\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\&quot;./Presentation1Black%20Box%20system%20testing.pptx\&quot; class\u003d\&quot;btn\&quot;\u003e📂 Download Presentation\u003c/a\u003e \u003c/div\u003e \u003c!-- Project 2 --\u003e \u003cdiv class\u003d\&quot;project-card\&quot;\u003e \u003ch3\u003eProject 2: Enterprise Hybrid Lab \u0026 Splunk SIEM Engineering\u003c/h3\u003e \u003cp\u003eDesigned a multi-site network lab within EVE-NG to evaluate zero-trust network layout boundaries. Simulated live Red Team penetration routing paths over an encrypted IPsec VPN tunnel while aggregating enterprise telemetry back to a central Splunk platform.\u003c/p\u003e \u003ch4\u003eCore Phases Execution:\u003c/h4\u003e \u003cul\u003e \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNetwork Isolation:\u003c/strong\u003e Programmed pfSense firewalls to contain lateral host movement.\u003c/li\u003e \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOffensive Auditing:\u003c/strong\u003e Ran custom vulnerability sequences against target systems and corporate web elements.\u003c/li\u003e \u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetection Engineering:\u003c/strong\u003e Engineered specialized Splunk Processing Language (SPL) rules to trigger immediate alerts on live attacks.\u003c/li\u003e \u003c/ul\u003e \u003cimg class\u003d\&quot;project-image\&quot; src\u003d\&quot;network-topology.png\&quot; alt\u003d\&quot;EVE-NG Network Topolog